	"about": {
		"text": "The Finnish soured milk drink, tart and thicker than milk. Pasteurised milk is fermented at 18–24 °C for 15–24 hours. It is also the buttermilk left from churning cultured cream (kirnupiimä). Western Finland traditionally made a stringy long piimä, eastern Finland a curdled one.",
