	"how": {
		"text": "Lactic acid bacteria sour the milk slowly at room temperature, giving a sour drink thicker than milk. Kirnupiimä is the related buttermilk from churning cultured cream. Lactococci make the acid, and the diacetylactis strains and Leuconostoc make diacetyl and CO₂ from citrate.",
